---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  site="Enclavetools"
  title="Server Certainty Blueprint | Real AI Hardware Benchmarks & Exact BOM"
  pageTitle="Server Certainty Blueprint"
  pageDescription="Get a Server Certainty Blueprint personalized to your AI model and traffic load: real quantized benchmarks (FP32/FP8/INT8), exact Bill of Materials with SKUs, NUMA-tuned vLLM/SGLang configs, zero-touch telemetry harness, and 3-year TCO analysis. $1,997 (total value $6,100) with a zero-touch speed guarantee."
  canonicalUrl="https://enclavetools.com/benchmark-offer"
  showSearch={false}
  showNav={false}
  showFooter={false}
  ogTitle="Server Certainty Blueprint: Real Benchmarks & Exact BOM for Your AI"
  ogDescription="Real quantized benchmarks, exact BOM with SKUs, NUMA-tuned deployment configs, and 3-year TCO analysis — personalized to your model and traffic load. $1,997 (value $6,100)."
  ogImage="https://enclavetools.com/og-benchmark-blueprint.png"
  ogUrl="https://enclavetools.com/benchmark-offer"
  ogType="product"
  ogSiteName="Enclavetools"
  twitterCard="summary_large_image"
  twitterTitle="Server Certainty Blueprint: Real Benchmarks & Exact BOM"
  twitterDescription="Real quantized benchmarks, exact BOM, tuned configs & TCO analysis for your AI model. $1,997 (value $6,100)."
  twitterImage="https://enclavetools.com/og-benchmark-blueprint.png"
  keywords={["AI hardware sizing", "GPU provisioning", "server benchmark service", "vLLM optimization", "MoE deployment", "exact Bill of Materials", "TCO analysis"]}
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div id="app">
      <!-- HEADER -->
      <h1
        class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold text-brand-forest tracking-tight mb-6 leading-tight text-center md:text-left"
      >
        Stop Guessing Hardware for <span
          class="text-brand-teal"
          id="displayModel">Your AI</span
        >.<br />
        Before It Costs You <span class="text-amber-500">Thousands</span>.
      </h1>

      <div
        class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-muted border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-5 mb-8 font-medium"
        id="subheadline"
      >
        You need <strong class="text-brand-forest" id="displayInTok"
          >4,000</strong
        > input tokens → <strong class="text-brand-forest" id="displayOutTok"
          >500</strong
        > output tokens, serving <strong
          class="text-brand-forest"
          id="displayUsers">10</strong
        > concurrent users at <strong class="text-brand-forest" id="displayRPS"
          >1</strong
        > RPS.
      </div>

      <!-- SPEC BADGE GRID -->
      <div
        class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 bg-brand-forest/5 p-5 md:p-6 rounded-2xl mb-10 border border-brand-forest/10"
      >
        <div
          class="bg-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium text-brand-muted border border-brand-forest/10 shadow-sm"
        >
          🧠 Model: <span class="text-brand-forest font-bold" id="badgeModel"
            >MiniMax-M3 (MoE)</span>
        </div>
        <div
          class="bg-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium text-brand-muted border border-brand-forest/10 shadow-sm"
        >
          ⚙️ Params: <span class="text-brand-forest font-bold" id="badgeParams"
            >428B</span>
        </div>
        <div
          class="bg-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium text-brand-muted border border-brand-forest/10 shadow-sm"
        >
          🎯 Mode: <span class="text-brand-forest font-bold" id="badgeMode"
            >Production Inference</span>
        </div>
        <div
          class="bg-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium text-brand-muted border border-brand-forest/10 shadow-sm"
        >
          📥 Load: <span class="text-brand-forest font-bold" id="badgeInTok"
            >7,000 Input / 1,000 Output</span>
        </div>
        <div
          class="bg-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium text-brand-muted border border-brand-forest/10 shadow-sm"
        >
          👥 Users: <span class="text-brand-forest font-bold" id="badgeUsers"
            >10 Concurrent</span>
        </div>
        <div
          class="bg-brand-forest text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-bold shadow-sm"
        >
          💾 Est. VRAM: <span class="text-white" id="badgeVram">~1,672 GB</span>
        </div>
        <div id="moeNote" class="hidden w-full text-xs text-amber-700 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl px-4 py-2">
          ⚡ MoE model detected — VRAM estimate reflects full weight loading but KV cache scaled to active parameters (~13% of total). Actual production VRAM may vary by quantization strategy.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- AGITATION -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-forest mt-12 mb-4">
        The <span class="text-amber-500">$100,000 Hardware Trap</span>
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg text-brand-muted mb-4">
        Calculating raw unquantized parameters for MiniMax-M3 tells you that you
        need <strong>1.6TB+ of VRAM</strong> just to hold the model.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-brand-muted mb-4">
        So companies do one of two things:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-8 mb-4 text-lg text-brand-muted space-y-3">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-red-600">They Over-Provision:</strong> They waste $50,000–$100,000
          buying massive, unoptimized GPU clusters, inflated rack space, and absurd
          power setups for capacity they will never use.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-red-600">They Under-Provision:</strong> They buy a budget
          rig, skip tuning their PCIe topology or CPU/NUMA nodes, and watch their
          server choke at 10 concurrent users—sending latency past 30 seconds until
          the API throws 503 errors.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <blockquote
        class="text-lg text-brand-muted font-medium my-6 border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-5"
      >
        Buying raw GPU memory without testing real-world quantization and bus
        bottlenecks is like buying a 50-passenger commercial bus just to drive
        yourself to work every morning.
      </blockquote>

      <p class="text-lg text-brand-muted font-medium">
        You don't need theoretical math. You need real hardware benchmarks under
        your exact traffic load.
      </p>

      <!-- OFFER -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-forest mt-12 mb-2">
        The <span class="text-amber-500"
          >Complete Server Certainty Blueprint</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6 text-lg">
        Custom-built for <strong class="text-brand-forest" id="offerModel"
          >MiniMax-M3 (MoE)</strong
        > at <strong class="text-brand-forest" id="offerUsers">10</strong> concurrent
        users. No generic forum posts or simulated spreadsheets. Just real benchmark
        data measured on bare-metal hardware.
      </p>

      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse my-8">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-brand-forest/10">
            <th
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 font-bold text-brand-forest"
              >#</th
            >
            <th
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 font-bold text-brand-forest"
              >Deliverable</th
            >
            <th
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 font-bold text-brand-forest"
              >Value</th
            >
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted">1</td
            >
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted"
              ><strong class="text-brand-forest"
                >The Quantized Benchmark Matrix</strong
              > — Real tokens/sec measured across 3 complete production builds (FP32
              baseline vs. optimized FP8/INT8 builds) under your exact 7,000/1,000
              token load.</td
            >
            <td
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted font-bold"
              >$2,500</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted">2</td
            >
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted"
              ><strong class="text-brand-forest"
                >Exact Bill of Materials (BOM)</strong
              > — Specific make, model, and SKUs for motherboard, CPU, RAM clock speeds,
              NVMe drives, PSU, chassis, and PCIe/NVLink layouts. Zero ambiguity.</td
            >
            <td
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted font-bold"
              >$2,000</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted">3</td
            >
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted"
              ><strong class="text-brand-forest"
                >"No-Bottleneck" Config Package</strong
              > — NUMA-node tuned, kernel-optimized vLLM/SGLang YAML deployment files
              ready to drop straight into production.</td
            >
            <td
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted font-bold"
              >$2,200</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted">4</td
            >
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted"
              ><strong class="text-brand-forest"
                >Zero-Touch Telemetry Harness</strong
              > — A private diagnostic validation script to verify your deployment
              internally without ever giving external parties root access.</td
            >
            <td
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted font-bold"
              >$1,300</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted">5</td
            >
            <td class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted"
              ><strong class="text-brand-forest">3-Year TCO Comparison</strong> —
              Pre-built vs. whitebox vs. cloud rentals. Shows your CFO exactly where
              to save $40k+ in long-term operational costs.</td
            >
            <td
              class="p-4 border border-brand-forest/10 text-brand-muted font-bold"
              >$1,500</td
            >
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p class="text-brand-muted font-bold text-lg mt-2">
        Total Value: <span class="text-amber-500">$9,500</span>
      </p>

      <!-- PRICE -->
      <div class="text-center my-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-forest mb-2">
          Today's Price
        </h3>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-2xl text-brand-muted line-through">$5,997</span>
          <p class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-amber-500">$2,997</p>
        </div>
        <p class="text-brand-muted mt-3 italic">
          A single avoided GPU purchase pays for this entire blueprint 10x over
          on day one.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- SOCIAL PROOF -->
      <div
        class="bg-brand-forest/5 border border-brand-forest/10 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl my-8 italic text-brand-muted relative"
      >
        <div
          class="absolute text-8xl text-amber-500/20 -top-4 left-4 font-serif"
        >
          "
        </div>
        <p class="relative z-10 text-lg">
          "We were quoted $110,000 for a pre-built AI server for our large model
          workload. This blueprint showed us an optimized dual-EPYC setup with
          proper PCIe routing that gave us 90% of the performance for less than
          half the cost — without blowing our power budget."
        </p>
        <span class="block mt-4 font-semibold text-brand-teal not-italic"
          >— Head of Infrastructure, Enterprise Logistics Firm</span
        >
      </div>

      <div
        class="bg-brand-forest/5 border border-brand-forest/10 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl my-6 italic text-brand-muted relative"
      >
        <div class="absolute text-8xl text-amber-500/20 -top-4 left-4 font-serif">"</div>
        <p class="relative z-10 text-lg">
          "We were about to sign a $180k PO for a vendor-configured GPU cluster. The blueprint showed us a whitebox dual-EPYC build that hit the same throughput for $67k — and the NUMA tuning configs worked first try."
        </p>
        <span class="block mt-4 font-semibold text-brand-teal not-italic"
          >— VP of Engineering, Series B AI Startup</span
        >
      </div>

      <div
        class="bg-brand-forest/5 border border-brand-forest/10 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl my-6 italic text-brand-muted relative"
      >
        <div class="absolute text-8xl text-amber-500/20 -top-4 left-4 font-serif">"</div>
        <p class="relative z-10 text-lg">
          "The quantized benchmark matrix made the hardware decision obvious. Our previous estimate had us buying 12× H100s. The INT8 benchmark showed 6× H100s hit our latency SLA with 40% headroom — exactly the number we needed for the board presentation."
        </p>
        <span class="block mt-4 font-semibold text-brand-teal not-italic"
          >— Platform Architect, Financial Services Firm</span
        >
      </div>

      <!-- GUARANTEE -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-forest mt-12 mb-4">
        The <span class="text-amber-500">Zero-Touch</span> Verified Speed Guarantee
      </h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted mb-4">
        We stand by our engineering <strong>100%</strong>. We guarantee our
        projected tokens/second throughput when deployed to our exact
        specifications.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-forest mt-6 mb-3">
        How The Zero-Touch Verification Script Works
      </h3>
      <p class="text-brand-muted mb-4">
        We never ask for root SSH access or entry into your private network. Here
        is how we verify performance while keeping your InfoSec team happy:
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-4 mt-4">
        <div
          class="flex gap-3 items-start bg-brand-forest/5 p-5 rounded-xl border border-brand-forest/10"
        >
          <span class="text-amber-500 font-extrabold text-lg shrink-0">1</span>
          <div class="text-brand-muted">
            <strong class="text-brand-forest">Deploy Your Specs:</strong> Build
            your server using our exact Bill of Materials (BOM) and apply our tuned
            configuration file.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex gap-3 items-start bg-brand-forest/5 p-5 rounded-xl border border-brand-forest/10"
        >
          <span class="text-amber-500 font-extrabold text-lg shrink-0">2</span>
          <div class="text-brand-muted">
            <strong class="text-brand-forest">Run 1-Line Audit:</strong> Run our
            open-source script locally in your environment:
            <div class="mt-2 space-y-2">
              <code class="block bg-brand-bg border border-brand-forest/10 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-brand-forest overflow-x-auto">curl -fsSL https://enclavetools.com/verify.sh -o verify.sh</code>
              <code class="block bg-brand-bg border border-brand-forest/10 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-brand-forest overflow-x-auto">cat verify.sh  # inspect before running</code>
              <code class="block bg-brand-bg border border-brand-forest/10 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-brand-forest overflow-x-auto">bash verify.sh</code>
              <p class="text-xs text-brand-muted/70 italic">No network calls home. No root access required. Read it first.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex gap-3 items-start bg-brand-forest/5 p-5 rounded-xl border border-brand-forest/10"
        >
          <span class="text-amber-500 font-extrabold text-lg shrink-0">3</span>
          <div class="text-brand-muted">
            <strong class="text-brand-forest">Inspect The Log:</strong> The script
            runs locally, inspects your GPU/CPU clock speeds, PCIe bus width,
            thermal states, and replays your exact token load. You can review the
            plain-text output before sending anything to us.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex gap-3 items-start bg-brand-forest/5 p-5 rounded-xl border border-brand-forest/10"
        >
          <span class="text-amber-500 font-extrabold text-lg shrink-0">4</span>
          <div class="text-brand-muted">
            <strong class="text-brand-forest">1-Click Refund:</strong> If the system
            matches our blueprint specs and misses our projected tokens/sec
            throughput, simply send the signed diagnostic file to
            <strong class="text-brand-forest">claims@enclavetools.com</strong> for
            an immediate 100% refund.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mt-6 italic">
        <strong class="text-amber-600">Note:</strong> The guarantee applies to systems
        deployed to our exact BOM specifications and environment configurations. Hardware
        modified outside the blueprint or throttled by facility cooling failures voids
        the refund claim, but still includes our Best-Effort Advisory support.
      </p>

      <!-- SCARCITY / CAPACITY -->
      <div class="text-center my-8">
        <div
          class="bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 px-6 py-3 rounded-full inline-block font-bold border border-emerald-200 shadow-sm"
        >
          📋 <span id="slotCount">4</span> benchmarking engagements open for this monthly cohort.
        </div>
        <p class="text-brand-muted text-xs mt-2 italic" id="slotUpdated"></p>
        <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mt-3">
          Full-system benchmarking requires renting high-end bare-metal clusters and running live stress tests under your specific parameters. Because testing schedules are bound to physical hardware availability, we cap deliveries at <strong
            id="slotCount2">4 client engagements per monthly cohort</strong
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="text-center mb-8">
        <a
          href="/contact"
          id="contactCtaBtn"
          class="btn-primary block w-full md:w-auto md:inline-block text-xl font-bold px-8 py-5 shadow-xl hover:scale-105 transition-transform text-center mx-auto"
        >
          ✅ YES — Reserve My Spot &amp; Generate My Blueprint
        </a>
        <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mt-4">
          Takes 90 seconds to submit your specs. No sales call required.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- PS -->
      <div class="border-t border-brand-forest/10 pt-8 mt-10 text-brand-muted">
        <strong class="text-amber-600">P.S.</strong> The cost of inaction: You order
        a pre-configured "AI Server," hit an undetected PCIe or NUMA bottleneck in
        month two, and burn <strong>$20k</strong> in senior engineer overtime trying
        to fix it. <strong id="psSlots">4 cohort openings available.</strong> Reserve your spot now.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script src="/scripts/benchmark-offer.js" defer></script>
</Layout>
